,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Is your feature request related to a problem?\n\nI'm trying to run mypy against a package that uses Ibis, but I get some errors. For example:\r\n\r\n```\r\nbigframes/series.py:8: error: Skipping analyzing \"ibis.expr.types\": module is installed, but missing library stubs or py.typed marker  [import]\r\nbigframes/dataframe.py:5: error: Skipping analyzing \"ibis.expr.types\": module is installed, but missing library stubs or py.typed marker  [import]\r\nbigframes/dataframe.py:5: note: See https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/running_mypy.html#missing-imports\r\nbigframes/engine.py:7: error: Skipping analyzing \"ibis\": module is installed, but missing library stubs or py.typed marker  [import]\r\n```\n\n### Describe the solution you'd like\n\nSince Ibis already type checks itself, I think it may be sufficient to add a `py.typed` file as a marker. See: https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/running_mypy.html#missing-library-stubs-or-py-typed-marker\n\n### What version of ibis are you running?\n\n4.0.0\n\n### What backend(s) are you using, if any?\n\nBigQuery\n\n### Code of Conduct\n\n- [X] I agree to follow this project's Code of Conduct","closed_by":{"login":"cpcloud","id":417981,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNzk4MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/417981?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpcloud","html_url":"https://github.com/cpcloud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpcloud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpcloud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpcloud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpcloud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.git